    <section id="journey" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>02.1 · route map</span>
        <h2>One tool call, three trust boundaries.</h2>
        <p>The current prompt loop is synchronous, but the data changes shape repeatedly. “Rust → Wasm → Rust” is only the middle of the trip.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="data-journey-map">
        <div class="journey-zone journey-zone-remote">
          <div class="journey-zone-label"><span>outside <code>dekopon-run</code></span><strong>model endpoint</strong></div>
          <div class="journey-node"><small>HTTP response</small><strong>tool call arguments</strong><code>JSON text inside JSON</code></div>
        </div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">↓</i>
        <div class="journey-zone journey-zone-host">
          <div class="journey-zone-label"><span>process · main OS thread</span><strong>Rust host</strong></div>
          <div class="journey-node-row">
            <div class="journey-node"><small><code>dekopon-model</code></small><strong><code>String</code></strong><code>function.arguments</code></div>
            <b aria-hidden="true">→ parse →</b>
            <div class="journey-node"><small><code>dekopon-run</code></small><strong><code>serde_json::Value</code></strong><code>must be object</code></div>
            <b aria-hidden="true">→ encode →</b>
            <div class="journey-node"><small>provider host</small><strong><code>String</code></strong><code>input_json</code></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">↓ canonical lower · UTF-8 bytes</i>
        <div class="journey-zone journey-zone-guest">
          <div class="journey-zone-label"><span>same process + calling thread · sandbox memory</span><strong>Wasm component</strong></div>
          <div class="journey-node-row">
            <div class="journey-node"><small>generated adapter</small><strong>WIT <code>string</code></strong><code>ptr + length</code></div>
            <b aria-hidden="true">→ parse →</b>
            <div class="journey-node"><small>guest Rust heap</small><strong><code>serde_json::Value</code></strong><code>Provider::invoke</code></div>
            <b aria-hidden="true">→ encode →</b>
            <div class="journey-node"><small>generated adapter</small><strong>response <code>String</code></strong><code>succeeded | failed</code></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">↑ canonical lift · then the path reverses</i>
      </div>

      <div class="article-callout callout-plain">
        <strong>Trust does not improve merely because syntax parsed.</strong>
        <p>The model’s tool name and arguments remain untrusted after JSON decoding. Guest output remains untrusted after canonical lifting and typed response decoding. Parsing proves shape, not truth, permission, or safety.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

